Round complete. Both deliverable files are written (impl/gen_rader.c via the impl→impl_7 symlink, and my strategy record), all gates pass at all 16 class sizes, the L=31 graded cell is bit-identical to r6 and unregressed, and the lease is released.

**Summary of the round** — I profiled before optimizing (new env-gated `RP_PROF` per-pass timer) and found the large-prime passes were **front-end bound, not memory bound**: `-funroll-loops` had peeled the blocked conv's inner loop into ~75 KB of straight-line code per chunk (past L1I), which is why cache-hot passes ran ~2.8x above the load-port model. Three shipped changes, zero arithmetic moved (every chain output cmp-bit-identical to r6): pinned-rolled conv tiles (−7% at p=89, −19% at 101, −8% at 113, −9..14% at 61), dead map-fusion arms compiled out of every generic kernel (~20 KB each, −0.6..1.8% more), and gen_layout's fold-prefetch recipe on the x-pass gated to p≥107 (−1.5% at 113, −0.5% at 127). I also closed three queued items by analysis rather than windows: x-band custody blocking is a no-op (the custody chain already sits at the 5-sweep/step memory floor), NT stores can't transfer to an in-place chain (no RFO to kill), and the p=19/127 Φ-split only reaches 7m² vs dense 9m² because its Karatsuba needs linear (not cyclic) convolutions — all recorded with the numbers/op-counts so nobody rediscovers them.

Front-end codegen repair + gated x-pass stream prefetch (no new arithmetic): **L=31 graded cell 84.82 µs/step at B=16 and 85.63 µs at B=1** (held-lease; bit-identical to r6), class duty now 61→1758 / 101→13546 (−21%) / 113→20170 (−11%) µs/step, **rel L2 4.06e-16 single, 1.78e-15 two-step** (tol 3e-14).
